; hearth-ask-send.fk — the discovering client: reads the BOARD, verifies
; the server stands, and sends — no paths told, no session knowledge.
; stdin lines: turn, kind, body text. A turn of 0 (or blank) asks the
; BODY for the next number (max turn on the task spool + 1) — hand-minted
; numbers collided when a killed sender's frame already sat on the spool
; (witnessed 2026-09-01, turn 9701 answered twice-asked).
; Multiline source packets use observe/hearth-ask-file-run.bml.
; preflight-exec: forbidden
; preludes: form-stdlib/bml/hearth-client.bml
(do
    (let turn0 (str_to_int (read_line)))
    (let kind (read_line))
    (hc-send turn0 kind (hc-body-line)))
